= The End of Garrick Crowde

With any hope of a political comeback shattered, Garrick Crowde has finally retired from public life. It’s likely that he abandoned any thought of challenging [+ royalist_leader +] long ago, if he ever entertained such an idea. The former pharmacist from a small Avrizan town simply lacks the ego and desire for power necessary to confront the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Royalist</span> leader.

In a brief meeting with Gorrick, Crowde agreed to withdraw from all political activity for two years and return to his previous profession as a pharmacist.

Meanwhile, Staal remains confident in a dangerous delusion—that [+ royalist_leader +] will act like a conventional party leader and offer concessions to maintain unity, and to join the cabinet to avoid new elections. He has done no such thing.